# The toolchain runs on Linux inside containers, so line endings are pinned to LF
# in both the repository and the working copy, regardless of the contributor's
# platform or their core.autocrlf setting.
#
# This is not cosmetic:
#   - CRLF in a .env file makes every value end in a stray \r, so APP_ENV becomes
#     "development\r" and fails validation at startup.
#   - CRLF breaks tab-indented recipes in a Makefile on Linux.
#   - CRLF in a shell script gives "bad interpreter" errors in a container.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
